18
00:00:51,350 --> 00:00:51,790
Morning.

19
00:00:52,470 --> 00:00:53,590
Hi there, Mr. Anderson.

20
00:00:54,270 --> 00:00:55,530
How are you on this fine morning?

21
00:00:55,850 --> 00:00:56,190
Fine.

22
00:00:57,750 --> 00:00:59,450
It sure is cold this morning, isn't it?

23
00:00:59,710 --> 00:01:01,190
I barely even got out of bed.

24
00:01:01,800 --> 00:01:04,200
Yeah, it's pretty cold, all right.

25
00:01:04,200 --> 00:01:05,490
Did you catch the news this morning?

26
00:01:05,950 --> 00:01:08,070
I heard that there was a fire in Byron Street.

27
00:01:08,580 --> 00:01:10,520
No, I didn't hear about that.

28
00:01:10,820 --> 00:01:12,920
Did you happen to watch the football game last night?

29
00:01:13,360 --> 00:01:15,560
The Patriots scored in the last minute.

30
00:01:15,560 --> 00:01:17,080
No, I don't like football.

31
00:01:18,260 --> 00:01:21,660
Oh, by the way, I saw you with your daughter at the office Christmas party.

32
00:01:22,160 --> 00:01:22,880
She's really beautiful.

33
00:01:23,600 --> 00:01:23,980
She's my wife.

34
00:01:24,600 --> 00:01:25,680
Oh, here's my floor.

35
00:01:26,280 --> 00:01:26,960
Nice talking to you.

36
00:01:27,280 --> 00:01:28,280
Goodbye.

37
00:01:28,280 --> 00:01:29,820
Oh, sir, this is the 56th floor.

38
00:01:30,320 --> 00:01:31,120
We're on the 70th.

39
00:01:31,340 --> 00:01:31,940
That's okay.

40
00:01:32,220 --> 00:01:33,140
I'll take the stairs.

41
00:01:38,230 --> 00:01:40,590
Okay, I think this guy was a little bit annoying.

42
00:01:41,170 --> 00:01:44,370
Yeah, Mr. Anderson really didn't want to talk to him, did he?

43
00:01:44,550 --> 00:01:45,710
Yeah, I think that was pretty obvious.

44
00:01:45,990 --> 00:01:47,370
He left the elevator in a hurry.

45
00:01:47,910 --> 00:01:50,510
Okay, let's take a look at our language today in Language Takeaway.

46
00:01:52,440 --> 00:01:53,440
Language Takeaway.

47
00:01:53,440 --> 00:01:56,080
All right, what do we have today in Language Takeaway?

48
00:01:56,300 --> 00:02:00,500
Well, we've got four words and phrases and our first one is barely even.

49
00:02:01,440 --> 00:02:01,960
Barely even.

50
00:02:02,620 --> 00:02:02,920
Barely even.

51
00:02:03,620 --> 00:02:04,920
So how do we use barely even?

52
00:02:05,200 --> 00:02:05,880
It's a little bit difficult.

53
00:02:06,100 --> 00:02:11,120
It's really similar to like almost couldn't or almost nothing or almost can't.

54
00:02:11,260 --> 00:02:13,320
So we use it usually in a negative sense.

55
00:02:13,980 --> 00:02:19,040
For example, I could say, I was so busy today, I could barely even eat my lunch.

56
00:02:19,360 --> 00:02:24,810
Okay, so I can maybe say, it was so dark, I could barely even see.

57
00:02:25,290 --> 00:02:26,470
Yeah, yeah.

58
00:02:26,760 --> 00:02:30,770
Or I'm so poor, I can barely even pay my rent.

59
00:02:31,320 --> 00:02:32,010
Okay, good.

60
00:02:32,920 --> 00:02:33,190
Barely even.

61
00:02:34,130 --> 00:02:35,490
All right, let's take a look at our next one.

62
00:02:36,600 --> 00:02:37,600
Catch.

63
00:02:37,600 --> 00:02:37,730
Catch.

64
00:02:38,600 --> 00:02:39,600
Catch.

65
00:02:39,600 --> 00:02:40,150
Did you catch the news?

66
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:43,870
So by did you catch the news, you mean did you hear the news?

67
00:02:44,480 --> 00:02:45,480
Exactly.

68
00:02:45,480 --> 00:02:46,250
So how else can we use this?

69
00:02:46,520 --> 00:02:47,520
Did you catch?

70
00:02:47,570 --> 00:02:50,350
A really common one is, I didn't catch your name.

71
00:02:50,630 --> 00:02:51,850
Yeah, I didn't hear your name.

72
00:02:51,930 --> 00:02:52,870
I didn't hear your name.

73
00:02:53,150 --> 00:02:55,870
Yeah, and we can also say, I didn't catch what he said.

74
00:02:56,170 --> 00:02:57,510
I didn't catch what he said, yeah.

75
00:02:57,810 --> 00:02:58,850
So I didn't hear.

76
00:02:59,360 --> 00:03:00,360
Yeah.

77
00:03:00,360 --> 00:03:01,150
Okay, let's look at our next word.

78
00:03:01,360 --> 00:03:02,640
By the way.

79
00:03:02,640 --> 00:03:03,130
By the way.

80
00:03:03,800 --> 00:03:04,490
By the way.

81
00:03:04,880 --> 00:03:05,370
By the way.

82
00:03:05,880 --> 00:03:12,640
Okay, so let's listen to some examples first of how we can use by the way and then we'll come back and talk more about it.

83
00:03:13,920 --> 00:03:16,720
Example one.

84
00:03:16,720 --> 00:03:18,200
Are you going to be at the meeting today?

85
00:03:18,640 --> 00:03:19,580
Yeah, I'll be there.

86
00:03:19,780 --> 00:03:22,140
Oh, by the way, did you hear what happened today?

87
00:03:25,880 --> 00:03:29,920
Example two.

88
00:03:29,920 --> 00:03:36,040
By the way, I almost forgot to tell you, Maggie called.

89
00:03:37,770 --> 00:03:44,750
Okay, so I see that when we say by the way, we're introducing a point after we've already talked about something.

90
00:03:45,030 --> 00:03:48,730
Exactly, and maybe it's not even related to the topic we were talking about.

91
00:03:48,790 --> 00:03:49,790
No, it's a different topic.

92
00:03:49,990 --> 00:03:50,830
Different topic, right?

93
00:03:51,010 --> 00:03:53,170
It's like saying, oh, I almost forgot to tell you.

94
00:03:53,330 --> 00:03:53,570
Exactly.

95
00:03:54,680 --> 00:03:56,930
So it's like, oh, Erica, don't forget we have a meeting today.

96
00:03:57,210 --> 00:03:59,110
Oh, and by the way, I like your new haircut.

97
00:03:59,730 --> 00:04:00,130
Thanks, Marco.

98
00:04:00,370 --> 00:04:00,930
All right, see?

99
00:04:01,520 --> 00:04:02,520
Yeah.

100
00:04:02,520 --> 00:04:03,520
That's the way you would use by the way.

101
00:04:03,530 --> 00:04:05,210
Okay, and our last word on language takeaway.

102
00:04:06,320 --> 00:04:06,810
Take the stairs.

103
00:04:07,400 --> 00:04:08,010
Take the stairs.

104
00:04:08,640 --> 00:04:09,470
Take the stairs.

105
00:04:09,820 --> 00:04:10,250
Take the stairs.

106
00:04:10,820 --> 00:04:12,070
So it doesn't mean you're going to take them somewhere.

107
00:04:12,350 --> 00:04:14,250
No, no, you're not taking them home with you.

108
00:04:14,550 --> 00:04:16,550
It means you're going to go up the stairs.

109
00:04:17,650 --> 00:04:19,010
Okay, so take the stairs.

110
00:04:19,350 --> 00:04:26,310
Yes, a lot of people might say use the stairs or go up the stairs, but our EnglishPod learners, they know, right?

111
00:04:26,570 --> 00:04:28,010
To use take the stairs.

112
00:04:28,280 --> 00:04:28,410
Yep.

113
00:04:29,280 --> 00:04:30,280
Take the stairs.

114
00:04:30,280 --> 00:04:32,330
Okay, so now we're ready to listen to our dialogue again.

115
00:04:32,920 --> 00:04:34,150
We're going to slow it down a little bit.

116
00:04:34,390 --> 00:04:37,070
And this will help you to catch these phrases a little bit better.

