145
00:06:03,750 --> 00:06:04,790
Let's start with the first one.

146
00:06:05,240 --> 00:06:07,160
It sure is cold this morning.

147
00:06:07,160 --> 00:06:08,550
It sure is cold.

148
00:06:09,400 --> 00:06:10,450
It sure is cold.

149
00:06:10,840 --> 00:06:11,950
It sure is cold.

150
00:06:12,430 --> 00:06:16,610
Okay, so we can change it up a little bit and say, it sure is hot.

151
00:06:17,520 --> 00:06:19,020
Or it sure is late.

152
00:06:19,460 --> 00:06:21,520
Okay, this sure is interesting.

153
00:06:22,440 --> 00:06:24,220
Or you could say, he sure is smart.

154
00:06:24,860 --> 00:06:27,500
So basically, you can change the adjective.

155
00:06:27,680 --> 00:06:28,680
Yes.

156
00:06:28,680 --> 00:06:29,940
Cold, hot, smart, hard, difficult.

157
00:06:30,520 --> 00:06:37,600
And when you say, sure is, this is a great way of emphasizing that you believe this adjective to be true.

158
00:06:37,600 --> 00:06:38,680
Okay, it sure is.

159
00:06:38,680 --> 00:06:40,000
Now what would be the answer to this?

160
00:06:40,280 --> 00:06:45,260
Well, in the dialogue, Mr. Anderson said, yeah, it's pretty cold, all right.

161
00:06:45,900 --> 00:06:47,580
It's pretty cold, all right.

162
00:06:47,800 --> 00:06:48,920
It's pretty cold, all right.

163
00:06:49,520 --> 00:06:54,640
So again, using the examples we used before, we can say, oh, it's pretty hot, all right.

164
00:06:55,480 --> 00:06:56,840
Or it's pretty late, all right.

165
00:06:57,400 --> 00:06:59,040
Or he's pretty smart, all right.

166
00:06:59,880 --> 00:07:01,240
Or this is pretty interesting, all right.

167
00:07:01,700 --> 00:07:03,120
So it means you're agreeing with that person.

168
00:07:03,400 --> 00:07:03,660
Exactly.

169
00:07:04,480 --> 00:07:04,620
Okay, great.

170
00:07:05,480 --> 00:07:09,980
So Marco, these things, it sure is blank and yeah, it's blank, all right.

171
00:07:10,500 --> 00:07:12,300
These can go together really well, can't they?

172
00:07:12,640 --> 00:07:15,340
